  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Expense Tracker App**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Android application\'s core functionality: tracking expenses by year and month. I\'m prioritizing the visual charts for budget and savings comparison. I need to make the user login and registration secure, and I\'ll include biometric fingerprint login support. My next steps involve designing the database structure to store this data efficiently.\n\n\n**Analyzing App UI Screens**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the user interface screens provided. The login screen uses a dark theme with a \"Control de Gastos\" title, offering email/password login and a registration link. It also features a JWT-secured API mention. The dashboard shows a user profile, logout, currency selection, and period filters (year/month). I\'m focusing on the component layout and user flow, to help design the navigation and API calls.\n\n\n**Reviewing Transaction Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now diving into the transaction breakdown screen\'s details. It includes \"EGRESOS TOTALES\" and two chart cards: one for cash flow (\"Historial de Flujo de Caja\") and another for expense distribution (\"Distribuci\303\263n de Gastos\"), currently showing placeholders for data. The lower portion\'s split-column layout presents \"Agregar Movimiento\" (expense/income input) and \"Nueva Categor\303\255a\" cards. The right column features a navigation tab for transaction history, categories, and mobile connectivity.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Personal Expense Control**\n\nI\'m now focusing on controlling personal expenses, with an emphasis on annual and monthly tracking. I want to include visual charts for budget and savings comparison. I need to make sure user login and password changes are secure. And I will integrate fingerprint login if the device supports it. I am using the provided images as a guide to help design the system.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am beginning the task by performing a Skill Check to identify relevant skills, and then I will read their instruction files to ensure I follow best practices for Jetpack Compose, Material 3 design, Room database integration, and custom app icon generation.\n\n### Skill Check\n- **android-secret-management**: [NOT RELEVANT] No external third-party API key is needed.\n- **app-icon-generation**: [RELEVANT] We should create a custom app icon representing Control de Gastos (wallet/finances).\n- **focus-mode**: [NOT RELEVANT] Not doing automated CSS selectors.\n- **frontend-design**: [RELEVANT] High priority. We must build a polished, modern, visual dark-themed Material 3 application that matches the provided images perfectly.\n- **gemini-api**: [NOT RELEVANT] No generative AI is requested.\n- **github-import-migration**: [NOT RELEVANT] No model migration needed.\n- **image-generation**: [NOT RELEVANT] Not requested.\n- **robolectric-testing**: [NOT RELEVANT] Not writing visual regression tests now.\n- **room-database-integration**: [RELEVANT] Very high priority. The app needs offline-capable storage for users, budgets, categories, and transactions (or \"movimientos\"), so Room is perfect here.\n\nI will read the instruction files for `room-database-integration`, `frontend-design`, and `app-icon-generation` first."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 786141273
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
