  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the ViewModel**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the ViewModel layer. Currently, my thought process revolves around active state management. I\'m exploring the components needed, and their structure. This layer will be key for interacting with the data, and I\'m keen on establishing the correct structure from the beginning.\n\n\n**Defining User State**\n\nI\'m now defining the user state within the ViewModel. I\'ve considered several properties, including the logged-in user, and period filters for year, month, and currency. Also, active tab management and the current budget are in focus. I\'m also planning the design for the UI states and the biometric support. I\'m thinking about how to integrate biometric authentication, and am considering the structure for a helper class or method in the MainActivity. I\'m checking the biometric requirements now.\n\n\n**Integrating Biometrics**\n\nI\'ve considered using `BiometricPrompt` and `BiometricManager` in Android, understanding that a `FragmentActivity` is needed. I plan to trigger the biometric modal from the UI via a callback in the composable. This approach maintains a clean architecture. My focus now is on designing the compose charts for financial visuals, specifically the historical cash flow chart.\n\n\n**Visualizing Financial Data**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to visualize financial data using custom Compose components. I\'m focusing on two key charts: a bar chart for monthly income/expenses and a donut chart (or a horizontal breakdown) for expense distribution. I\'m considering using Canvas for a custom, visually appealing implementation that complements the dashboard\'s style, for a highly readable display. I\'m also planning the \"Ahorrado/Restante\" display.\n\n\n**Planning Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now outlining the input fields needed. For user registration, it\'s email, password, and confirmation, and password resets will use either old and new passwords or a forgotten password reset. I\'m focusing on simplicity, allowing for easy registration, password changes, and resets via email. Transaction input includes amount, currency, description, category ID, and date. For category management, I\'ll need name and expense type. Budget updates will use month, year, and amount.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am now building the ViewModel class in `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/viewmodel/ExpenseViewModel.kt` to coordinate the business logic. It handles secure login, custom registration, password changes, biometric toggle states, and currency exchange rate arithmetic (Soles \360\237\207\265\360\237\207\252 vs Dollars \360\237\207\272\360\237\207\270 at 1 USD = 3.75 PEN). It gathers database entities, performs reactive calendar period filtering, and generates calculated values for visual graphics."
