  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Biometric Triggering**\n\nI\'m currently focused on triggering biometric authentication via `BiometricPrompt` in Android. The initial step involves verifying device capabilities and support using `BiometricManager.from(context).canAuthenticate()`. My immediate next steps are to figure out the code to trigger it.\n\n\n**Refining Biometric Prompt**\n\nI\'ve got the `BiometricPrompt` code ready for biometric login dialog prompting now. The core components include an executor, the `BiometricPrompt` itself, and an `AuthenticationCallback` to handle success. My immediate next step will be to make sure the app activity extends `FragmentActivity` for this code to work, and I\'ll adapt my code now to that end. I need to make a quick adjustment and verification.\n\n\n**Confirming FragmentActivity Integration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed `FragmentActivity` availability and now plan to refactor `MainActivity` to inherit it. My goal is a comprehensive `MainActivity.kt` with integrated screens. I\'m focusing on the login screen, aiming for a dark, elegant UI matching the reference image. Crucially, I\'m designing for a biometric/fingerprint login trigger, either as a floating button or integrated directly within the login form, likely next to the password input. This will streamline the login process.\n\n\n**Designing Screen Transitions**\n\nI\'m now outlining screen navigation flow for user registration and password management, focusing on seamless transitions. I plan to incorporate links to a standard register screen with fields for email, password, and confirmation, and a \"Change Password\" screen to enable updating user key hashes. I\'m thinking of a secure footer with a shield icon. I am trying to refine the process of navigating between screens and updating passwords.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI design. I\'m focusing on the main screen elements: a user profile area with a \"Logout\" button, a currency selector for \"Soles (S/)\" and \"D\303\263lares ($)\", and a period filter banner with dropdowns for year and month. I envision three elegant cards for balances, displaying \"BALANCE GENERAL\", \"INGRESOS TOTALES\", and \"EGRESOS TOTALES\" with custom icons. I\'m also planning a form for monthly budget management.\n\n\n**Visualizing Transaction Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the custom charts. I envision a grid layout with two key cards. The first card will show a \"Historial de Flujo de Caja\" with a double bar chart for income vs. expenses per month. If data is sparse, I\'ll display \"No hay suficientes datos hist\303\263ricos a\303\272n\" with a micro sine-wave chart. The second card will visualize the \"Distribuci\303\263n de Gastos\" as a donut chart with a legend and a progress badge comparing budget to savings. I\'ll include a message \"Registra gastos para ver la distribuci\303\263n aqu\303\255\" if no expenses are registered.\n\n\n**Defining Transaction Forms**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Registrar Gasto/Ingreso\" form. It\'ll feature a description field for the transaction, a dynamic category dropdown, and a compact date picker pre-filled with today\'s date. A large button will submit the entry. I\'m also planning a new category form with a text input, radio selectors for expense/income, and a gradient \"Create Category\" button. I\'m focusing on user-friendliness.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Biometric Prompt**\n\nI\'m now integrating biometric authentication in Compose, focusing on seamless user experience in emulated environments. I will be checking the successful package import, and triggering biometrics within a clickable button. I\'ll include logic to detect unsupported or unenrolled biometrics and then show a dialog that lets the user seamlessly mock/toggle fingerprint simulation. This approach ensures a smooth flow regardless of the device context.\n\n\n**Simulating Biometric Input**\n\nI\'m now designing an offline biometric simulation for testing. The plan is to display a custom dialog with a \"Simulate Fingerprint\" button. Clicking this button triggers a successful authentication. This design ensures users can test biometric login even on emulators without a fingerprint sensor and meets user criteria to enable testing of \"fingerprint login\". I\'ll also check the imports for the `MainActivity` including `androidx.fragment.app.FragmentActivity`.\n\n\n**Confirming `FragmentActivity`**\n\nI\'m verifying that `FragmentActivity` is accessible via our imports, and confirming its compatibility. I\'ll inherit `MainActivity` from `FragmentActivity` to avoid any dependency conflicts, and I\'ll keep the design for the UI layout and state-driven Compose application inside the single `MainActivity.kt` file. I\'m focusing on crafting a cohesive structure, to keep all dependencies local, and maintain a seamless compilation.\n\n\n**Organizing App Structure**\n\nI\'m now determining whether to organize reusable Composables into separate files or maintain them within `MainActivity.kt`. I\'ve decided a single `MainActivity.kt` file with clear sections for `MainActivity` (entry point), different screens (`AuthenticationScreen`, `RegisterScreen`, etc.), and component elements (forms, charts) is the best plan of attack. It\'ll be a self-contained masterpiece. I am confident that the single file approach will reduce compile errors and simplify updates. I\'ve also verified the essential biometric imports.\n\n\n**Designing Compose UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a comprehensive Compose UI. I\'ll create `CashFlowChart`, a bar list comparing incomes and expenses, and an `ExpenseDonutChart` for category distribution. I\'ll add tab controllers for transaction history, category listing, and connectivity info. Crucially, I\'m integrating a \"fingerprint login\" toggle within the profile chip or dashboard footer.\n\n\n**Implementing Biometric Triggers**\n\nI\'m now integrating the biometric trigger within the login credentials box with a fingerprint icon button. Clicking this triggers the `BiometricPrompt` if the device supports it, or launches a fingerprint simulation overlay as a fallback. I\'ve written the `checkBiometricSupport` function to verify biometric compatibility, and now I\'m building out both the native biometric check and the simulated fingerprint scanner to handle scenarios without hardware.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now write the full implementation of `/app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt`. It implements:\n1. **Inheritance from `FragmentActivity`**: Allowing `BiometricPrompt` to display seamlessly on Android devices.\n2. **Secure Login Screen**: Exactly matching Image 1 with real username-password checks, register options, change password forms, and custom styled inputs.\n3. **Fingerprint Authentication Button**: Triggers the real `BiometricPrompt` API. If biometric hardware is absent (such as in-emulator previews), it elegantly launches a beautiful, interactive fingerprint scanner overlay so the functionality can be demonstrated and tested.\n4. **Interactive Period Filtering**: Live dropdown filters for Year and Month, updating core dashboard computations in real-time.\n5. **Dynamic Metrics Cards**: Active General Balance, Income and Expenses totals in local Soles (`S/`) or Dollars (`$`), instantly converted dynamically on tap.\n6. **Custom Visual Components via Canvas**:\n   - *Historial de Flujo de Caja*: A bar graph comparing income and expenses.\n   - *Distribuci\303\263n de Gastos (Donut Chart)*: Interactive percentage indicator comparing expenses with a monthly preset budget.\n7. **Complete Transaction Management**: Adding and deleting records interactively.\n8. **Dynamic Categories Integration**: Creating custom expense or income categories on the fly.\n9. **Simulation Info panel**: Simulates JWT and mobile-connectivity sync details, highlighting modular decouple architectures as shown in the screenshots."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 670866855
    }
