    thinking: "**Confirming Application Settings**\n\nI have verified that both configurations are correctly set to \"Control de Gastos.\" Now, I\'m shifting focus to identify additional areas within the codebase that might benefit from refinement. Specifically, I\'ve checked and updated `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/theme/Color.kt` and `/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/theme/Theme`.\n\n\n**Reviewing Visual Architecture**\n\nI\'ve just finished a visual architecture check. Theme styling looks good: background, elevated surfaces, primary purple, success, and expense colors are all as intended. I\'ve confirmed appropriate sizes for the navigation bar and dividers. Plus, I ensured smooth screen transitions with AnimatedContent and the crossfade. Finally, fingerprint authentication is working.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully implemented the elegant **\"Sophisticated Dark\"** theme throughout the app!\n\n### Visual Identity & Theme Architecture\n- **Aesthetic Background Palette**: Swapped out the previous cosmic space navy theme for a polished, dark slate backplate (`#1C1B1F`) with elevated charcoal container elements (`#2B2930`) and modern borders (`#49454F`).\n- **Chic Theme Accents**: Incorporated subtle and beautiful color contrasts matching Material Design 3 guidelines:\n  - **Primary Lavender Highlight**: `#D0BCFF`\n  - **Muted Slate/Silver Details & Titles**: `#CAC4D0` / `#E6E1E5`\n  - **Luminous Mint (Income & Balances)**: `#80F3B9`\n  - **Soft Crimson/Pink (Expenses)**: `#F2B8B5`\n- **Balanced Component Contrast**: Updated the `onPrimary`, `onSecondary`, and `onTertiary` layout colors so that text placed on buttons or highlighted badges achieves optimal Material 3 typographic hierarchy and high accessibility standards.\n\n### Structural Updates & Fixes\n- **Robust Layout Adaptations**: Resolved three key compilation errors inside `MainActivity.kt`:\n  1. Loaded the proper `androidx.compose.ui.text.font.FontFamily` reference for the monospace details block.\n  2. Aligned elements cleanly in the Column overlay by correctly using `Modifier.align(Alignment.Start)` instead of the invalid `alignSelf` parameter on the target `Text` component.\n  3. Replaced the outdated `Divider` implementation with high-contrast Material 3 `HorizontalDivider` utilizing correct `thickness` parameters.\n- **Complete Feature Retention**: Perfectly preserved the existing secure login, simulated high-security biometric fingerprint scanner, decoupled API connection, multi-currency display toggle, custom budget configurations, interactive dynamic transaction forms, and detailed month-by-month database analytics."
